# RNRG — redirect map for the migration from the old site.
#
# Format: Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_redirects`. If the site stays on GitHub Pages,
# these must be reproduced as meta-refresh stubs instead, because GitHub Pages cannot
# issue a real 301 — see docs/migration.md.
#
# Rule: no old URL is deleted without a destination. Every line below was a real,
# reachable page on the previous site.

# ---- The two disconnected properties merge into one site ----
/energy                      /electrical/                 301
/energy/                     /electrical/                 301
/energy/*                    /electrical/                 301

# ---- Solar branch ----
/solar.html                  /solar/                      301
/solutions.html              /solar/                      301
/projects.html               /projects/                   301
/CompatibilityCheck.html     /quote/?track=solar          301

# The savings calculator was withdrawn: it multiplied any bill by 0.9 and presented the
# result as guaranteed savings. Its traffic has genuine solar intent, so it goes to the
# compatibility check rather than to a dead end.
/solar-calculator.html       /quote/?track=solar          301

# ---- Company ----
/about.html                  /about/                      301
/contact.html                /contact/                    301
/success.html                /thank-you/                  301

# ---- Testimonial collection: two duplicate forms merge into one ----
/recommendation.html         /reviews/#submit             301
/m.html                      /reviews/#submit             301

# ---- Abandoned draft ----
/new.html                    /solar/                      301

# ---- Legacy asset paths, kept so old links in messages and posts still resolve ----
/assets/img/*                /images/:splat               301
